{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities","id":1164747,"title":"Sidereal Caste Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-03T02:18:13-08:00","id":1164747,"title":"Sidereal Caste Abilities","content":"Quite a long time ago, Vance posted his current thoughts on Sidereal caste abilities, and said he was interested to see what people thought. But there was never any real discussion about it, so I thought I'd start a thread about it.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Journeys:</b> Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> <b>Serenity: </b>Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize<br /> <b>Battles:</b> Archery, Brawl, Melee, Presence, War<br /> <b>Secrets: </b>Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth<br /> <b>Endings: </b>Athletics, Awareness, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine</span><br /> <br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> And also, all Sidereals have Martial Arts as favoured. <br /> <br /> First, I think that giving them all Martial Arts as favoured is a great idea, since 90% of Sidereal PCs would just end up wanting it anyway. Though I wonder if they'll still have to get the Martial Arts merit.<br /> I kind of think maybe they should get it for free: part of the point of the Martial Arts merit, as I understood it, was that Martial Arts was just so good that it needed gating. But Sidereals are actually worse at martial arts than Solars because they (I assume) don't get Mastery. And its thematic.<br /> Still, that's slightly off-topic.<br /> <br /> So back to the main abilities.<br /> <br /> Journeys, Serenity and Secrets are all the same as in 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> What's been moved is that Battles have got Brawl, and lost Athletics to Endings (since their Martial Arts is now shared by everyone).<br /> <br /> I don't think this is terrible: Brawl does, I think, fit better with Battles than Endings.<br /> <br /> But I don't really see Athletics as fitting with Endings. I'm not really seeing much connection there: what does running, jumping and lifting have to do with ending stuff? Whereas Medicine obviously does.<br /> <br /> It fits better with Battles. Also, consider that now with Brawl and no Athletics, Battles has 4/5 of the same abilities as Dawn Castes (which I always assumed was something the designers were deliberately ignoring).<br /> <br /> But thinking about it more... should it really be in Battles either? I mean, it's Athletics. It's previous versions included charms like &quot;run without tiring&quot;. Shouldn't it be in Journeys?<br /> <br /> I'd therefore suggest that maybe Thrown should be Endings one combat ability. I think it's fitting for fate ninjas whose theme is ending stuff to throw shuriken or knives at people, and, you know, end them.<br /> <br /> That does mean Journeys no longer has one of the main combat abilities, but they'll have Athletics and Resistance (whereas Serenity just has Dodge and Secrets doesn't really have any combat stuff).<br /> <br /> For a more out-there alternative, Athletics could stay in Battles and Endings could get Melee. It might seem odd for Battles to not have Melee, but the executioner's axe, the assassin's blade, the sword that cuts the Gordian knot, could be in Endings. And with Archery, Athletics, Brawl, Presence and War, the Chosen of Mars still have plenty to do in fights while not having the same abilities as Dawn Castes (which I've always assumed is the reason they have Presence, frankly).<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not really saying &quot;I think this selection of Abilities is awful for Sidereals, and must change!&quot; Just giving possible suggestions. What do the rest of you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T03:56:05-08:00","id":1164751,"title":"","content":"The corebook mentions that Sidereals have their own methods of unlocking the Mastery effects. It'd be odd if the Exalt group canonically stated to be the most enlightened and best Martial Artists didn't get Mastery somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T04:01:51-08:00","id":1164752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities#post1164747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't really see Athletics as fitting with Endings. I'm not really seeing much connection there: what does running, jumping and lifting have to do with ending stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div> With Athletics (and Martial Arts), Awareness, Bureaucracy, Integrity, and Medicine as their auspicious abilities, the Chosen of Endings are basically <i>monks ... of death (and taxes)</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T04:22:55-08:00","id":1164754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164751#post1164751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The corebook mentions that Sidereals have their own methods of unlocking the Mastery effects. It'd be odd if the Exalt group canonically stated to be the most enlightened and best Martial Artists didn't get Mastery somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's Sutra-related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T04:38:07-08:00","id":1164757,"title":"","content":"I can see where you are coming from, for sure<br /> <br /> But I think that the set-up we've been shown is pretty solid. I can see myself playing any of those Castes, and that's a good thing. Also I think that to an extent, giving Athletics to Journeys is almost... it's too easy? Sidereals are all about the abstract, lateral associations. I think that making Athletics endings kind of suits in that Athletics is all about getting you somewhere and ending a movement, whereas Journeys are all about the Journey, so to speak. That works for me.<br /> <br /> Endings are my favourite though, and always have been, and I'm not a huge fan of Thrown, so maybe that's why I like it however hahaha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T05:28:30-08:00","id":1164761,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think there is no way to map 3E's abilities to 1E constellations. The Mast has nothing to do with Resistance (if I had to pair it with a 3E ability, it would be Integrity, but even that is sort of an awkward fit). War should obviously be The Banner, but that leaves us with no constellation for Presence. The Sword can't really be anything but Martial Arts (I mean, it could be Melee, but then you have nothing for The Spear <i>and </i>you have to rewrite the entirety of Sidereal Melee from the ground up). You could <i>maybe</i> say that The Gauntlet now corresponds to Presence (it's not a <i>terrible</i> fit thematically) and The Sword is Brawl, but let's face it, mapping an ability that can't use swords <i>at all </i>to that constellation would be... strange, to say the least. You could possibly make it work, because sids are supposed to be strange, but it still feels wrong.<br /> <br /> So I guess the least terrible solution I could come up with would be the following:<br /> <br /> - everybody has MA as favored<br /> - Journeys: Integrity, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> - Serenity: Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize<br /> - Battles: Archery, Melee, Presence, Resistance, War<br /> - Secrets: Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth<br /> - Endings: Athletics, Awareness, Brawl, Bureaucracy, Medicine<br /> <br /> (My <i>preferred</i> solution, of course, would be hiring Jenna Moran on the Sid book and letting her sort the whole mess out.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 12-03-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T05:45:05-08:00","id":1164762,"title":"","content":"I have to say, Martial Arts as favoured for all Siddies sounds 100% for me, because every PC is going to probably take it anyway, given how good and widely used MAs are and SMAs presumably will be.<br /> <br /> I wonder what SMAs will look like these days actually. Will they be notably powerful high Essence MA trees? Or will they take another kind of form? I was reading my 1e book this morning over breakfast and I was very tempted to see what Prismatic Arrangement of Creation looks like in 3e. The initial Magical Material Charms are pretty easy to translate but I can easily see stuff like &quot;your unarmed attacks are light artifact weapons&quot; being relatively high Essence simply because, like, wow that's powerful and it's, like, an opening charm in the form. Also will they require mastery of a &quot;lesser&quot; style? That would be cool, but we didn't want all the awesome shit to be locked behind high Essence requirements in 3e (though if any Exalt was going to do that, it would be Sidereals what with them having a lot of masters in their fictional power block).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:41:25-08:00","id":1164798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities#post1164747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I don't really see Athletics as fitting with Endings. I'm not really seeing much connection there: what does running, jumping and lifting have to do with ending stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death is coming for you and there is <i>nothing</i> you can do to outrun it.<br /> <br /> Athletics was Endings in 1st ed., wasn't it? Giving it back to Endings so Battles can get Brawl makes things fit rather nicely. A lot of it is going to depend on how Sidereal Charms are rebuilt though. The Charmsets in 2nd ed. have an interesting <i>premise</i>, but there's not much we can extrapolate from the execution. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T09:23:52-08:00","id":1164809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities#post1164747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I don't really see Athletics as fitting with Endings. I'm not really seeing much connection there</div> </div> </div> </div>Once, there was a maiden...<br /> ... who learned that the faster she ran, the faster she could run.<br /> Thus, running consumed her,<br /> \u200buntil, one day she ran beyond the ending of her life.<br /> &quot;And here I thought it would last forever,&quot; she said.<br /> \u200b&quot;But-&quot;<br /> \u200b&quot;There's always an ending,&quot; said the run.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe First Edition Sidereal Athletics Charms were primarily about things such as enhancing your motion by burning up your lifespan, whether literally or metaphorically, as well as a few effects to hasten things towards their conclusion.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, I find it to have resonance with the number of stories I've heard about athletes putting their bodies under so much strain that their hearts exploded in their thirties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what does running, jumping and lifting have to do with ending stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, think about what Dodge or Craft means for Serenity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T09:26:10-08:00","id":1164810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe First Edition Sidereal Athletics Charms were primarily about things such as enhancing your motion by burning up your lifespan, whether literally or metaphorically, as well as a few effects to hasten things towards their conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes more sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T09:54:25-08:00","id":1164816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164798#post1164798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death is coming for you and there is <i>nothing</i> you can do to outrun it.<br /> <br /> Athletics was Endings in 1st ed., wasn't it? Giving it back to Endings so Battles can get Brawl makes things fit rather nicely. A lot of it is going to depend on how Sidereal Charms are rebuilt though. The Charmsets in 2nd ed. have an interesting <i>premise</i>, but there's not much we can extrapolate from the execution.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Athletics was indeed Endings in 1e.<br /> <br /> It actually is helpful to remember the different edition Abilties and that helps in turn think on the associations. <br /> <br /> <b>Exalted: the Sidereals</b><br /> <i>Journeys: </i>Endurance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> <i>Serenity</i>: Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize<br /> <i>Battles:</i> Archery, Brawl, Melee, Presence, Resistance<br /> <i>Secrets</i>: Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth<br /> <i>Endings:</i> Athletics, Awareness, Bureaucracy, Martial Arts, Medicine<br /> <br /> <b>Manual of Exalted Power: Sidereals</b><br /> <i>Journeys:</i> Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> <i>Serenity:</i> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize<br /> <i>Battles:</i> Archery, Athletics, Melee, Presence, War<br /> <i>Secrets:</i> Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth<br /> <i>Endings:</i> Awareness, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Martial Arts, Medicine<br /> <br /> As a bonus, in early 2e Jenna Moran (who wrote the original Sidereal Charmset) had her own ideas on what they should have in 2e. And for that, she was of an opinion that the Sidereal set should basically be the case that the merged Abilities went to Journeys and Endings, and Battles picked up <i>both</i> the Abilities intorduced that edition. This would result in the following for Mercury, Mars, and Saturn's Chosen; Integrity would pick up the Scripture of the Drowning Maiden and apparently she was just fine with re-jiggering and rewriting the Presence tree to fit the Shield's scripture if need be. 2e was isntead written as usual 2e copy-paste, but that's another story to bitch aobut.<br /> <br /> <b>Jenna Moran's Proposed</b> 2e Set<br /> <i>Journeys:</i> Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> <i>Battles:</i> Archery, Integrity, Melee, Presence, War<br /> <i>Endings:</i> Athletics Awareness, Bureaucracy, Martial Arts, Medicine<br /> <br /> <b>Proposed 3e Set</b><br /> <i>Journeys:</i> Resistance, Ride, Sail, Survival, Thrown<br /> <i>Serenity:</i> Craft, Dodge, Linguistics, Performance, Socialize<br /> <i>Battles:</i> Archery, Brawl, Melee, Presence, War<br /> <i>Secrets:</i> Investigation, Larceny, Lore, Occult, Stealth<br /> <i>Endings:</i> Athletics Awareness, Bureaucracy, Integrity, Medicine<br /> <i>All:</i> Martial Art<br /> <br /> Okay, so what's the 3e set look like? IN a way it's kind of a split difference. This time Martial Arts is kind of pulled from anyone having it special, and Brawl is back. So Mars keeps Brawl, but doesn't get Integrity, it instead filling in for its place in Ending's gap.<br /> <br /> I think a few things need to be considered as the devs write things. One is that to some extent, the Charm structure for Sidereals in 1e can't really be held in contxt of current Charms. That is to say, I don't think there being a Charm per scripture line is something we'll see again, if only because 3e has a general feel of avoiding &quot;This Ability has four Charms and you're done.&quot; This is why a lot of Sidreals burned a favored on MAs or Occult no matter what, afterall. So I think we'll porobably see bigger Sidereal Charm trees. Not necssarily Solar or DB big, but bigger enough that there might be more to get to those ultimates, or something. This in itself probably opens some space to incorerate older effects and also expand Abilities for Sidsereals.<br /> <br /> I think a big thing that might end up is some Charmsets just get tossed out and written froms cratch, with maybe some extras tossed in to help. Here's what I mean on that. Take Resistance. A big issue wiht it in 2e is that it was kind of jus tthe 1e Endurance and Reistance trees glued together, with not a lot done to the former Battles Charms to make them fit in the Journeys flavor. I think here, And some of the Endurance Charms got transported over to Athletics, which made it even messier. And so on.<br /> <br /> Likely what'll happen is we see Resistance kind of just ripped apart and reevaluated. Many Charms might not reappear at all, replaced with ones that fit it better. Effects that are iconic, It also probably will just mean a shuffle on what Abilitty is associatedw ith what constellation. But I think if one was willing ot accept hey, maybe we end up with Integrity Charms based on the Drwning Maiden as something that could of happened, I don't see how it's not possible to make Integrity Charms based on the Scripture of the Expectant Maiden<br /> <br /> Sidereals are weird in that they have some very specific things based on the mechancis of the game and their homologues in the setting that other Exalts I don't think really feel in the same way. But I think it's also worth remembering is thes relationships are arbitrary, and while they were well tuned in 1e, doens't mean that changes are bad unless they're done in a lazy (or as at times I feel, hostile) fashion as the 2e adaptation did things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T09:56:06-08:00","id":1164818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164810#post1164810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to that, Athletics had the Rising Smoke as its constellation, which when you read the Scripture of the Maiden and the Dust, makes a lotta sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:03:31-08:00","id":1164820,"title":"","content":"What was it, 3 days less life per point of strength, dex or stamina added until the end of the scene? Something like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:12:27-08:00","id":1164821,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer to see Resistance in Endings, swapped for Athletics in Journeys. &quot;I/you have to live through this so that I die when I should&quot; defenses vs. disease that are applicable unless the Sidereal/target is fated to suffer it, and &quot;I can lift this heavy obstacle out the way of my journey, or yours&quot; both seem thematic enough to write a charm tree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:15:04-08:00","id":1164822,"title":"","content":"Athletics could have gone to Journeys, with Resistance remaining with Battles, and Presence going to Endings.<br /> <br /> Presence had already lost most of its Charms with the introduction of War, and the Sword lost its Charms with Violet Bier of Sorrows becoming just another Martial Art Style.<br /> <br /> So, Presence could be assigned to the constellation of the Sword.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Integrity could go to Journeys, since it's what replaced First Edition's Endurance, and it does the best job of representing Endurance's commitment to a goal.<br /> <br /> Resistance would remain with Battles, Athletics would go back to Endings, and once again, Presence would also go to Endings, under the constellation of the Sword.<br /> <br /> <br /> But if Integrity goes to the Sword, it's probably an executioner's sword. The Charms represent how the Sidereals need kill their compassion to fulfill Yu-Shan's callous designs, which often includes killing or causing death or not preventing the deaths that they could.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:19:58-08:00","id":1164825,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>, this feels kind of a bit of cruel thing for me to say, but did your OP just say something to the effect that can be paraphrased as &quot;Endings should get Thrown, because it's a ninja ability, and not Athletics, because it isn't!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ninjas are, in pop culture (pop culture versions of ninjas), sort of all kindsa jumpy and stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:22:09-08:00","id":1164826,"title":"","content":"Endings should get Athletics because it's in the 1e book and super cool, like most things in that most excellent book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:36:38-08:00","id":1164829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164825#post1164825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>, this feels kind of a bit of cruel thing for me to say, but did your OP just say something to the effect that can be paraphrased as &quot;Endings should get Thrown, because it's a ninja ability, and not Athletics, because it isn't!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ninjas are, in pop culture (pop culture versions of ninjas), sort of all kindsa jumpy and stuff!</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Thrown is about killing things, and Athletics is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway, Isator makes a fair point about the charms themselves. As I said, I wasn't saying &quot;I'm definitely sure these ability selections are rubbish&quot;, just so much that I wasn't sure, and thought I'd open it for discussion since Vance wondered what people thought.<br /> <br /> But it seems people are pretty happy with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T12:30:11-08:00","id":1164845,"title":"","content":"I could readily imagine that Athletics was the kind of thing that wound up with Endings just as a result of the shuffle, and then Jenna worked to make it thematic and compelling through the theme of that Caste.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's not to say that it wasn't something that was attached from the outset, just speculation that it's possible to make just about any of them work in any Caste if you've got good ideas.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, with an already existing example of what Athletics can mean in Endings, I think that makes a stronger idea than it being in Journeys. Certainly, I'd say that the Endings Abilities in general are an exercise in giving the Caste nuance that it would probably lack if it had the Abilities and themes that most people would expect. That can probably be said with any of the Castes, but is most acute for the one concerned with mortality and inevitability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T00:17:52-08:00","id":1164982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164845#post1164845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could readily imagine that Athletics was the kind of thing that wound up with Endings just as a result of the shuffle, and then Jenna worked to make it thematic and compelling through the theme of that Caste.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's not to say that it wasn't something that was attached from the outset, just speculation that it's possible to make just about any of them work in any Caste if you've got good ideas.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, with an already existing example of what Athletics can mean in Endings, I think that makes a stronger idea than it being in Journeys. Certainly, I'd say that the Endings Abilities in general are an exercise in giving the Caste nuance that it would probably lack if it had the Abilities and themes that most people would expect. That can probably be said with any of the Castes, but is most acute for the one concerned with mortality and inevitability.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Athletics: it's also important to note that Athletics isn't just the ninja jump and ninja run ability. It also contains superior strength through lifting or breaking. Solars (humor me) also express Athletics through various methods of improving their combat capabilities.<br /> <br /> An Endings expression of Athletics could be an embodiment of eventuality and the forward march of time. It can represent how all things crumble to dust in the grasp of ages. It can call forth the swift end that all forms of motion face. It can also burn away the Chosen's own life force or consume their focus burning away other details for the chase.<br /> <br /> I imagine a possible charm tree for Feats of Strength starting with a basic boost for counting strength higher for minimums. Then from there a charm that enhances suffering objects. Eventually I could see an essence 5 charm that could turn let you break an intimacy by tightly grasping a mortals hand. Maybe even end an abstract concept or break strange things normally not capable of being suffered by strength, like literally breaking enchantments. Though that's the Feats of Strength sub-tree I'm thinking about, and likely a sub-branch of that. Strength enhancing is pretty easy to think about when it comes to how to end things.<br /> <br /> Charms that enhances chases are obvious. You're chasing them to end them. Maybe weird combat charms that let chases enhance a decisive attack? Nah, not too interesting but.... Hmmm...<br /> <br /> Leaping lends well to flashy assassin ninjas of course.<br /> <br /> The combat boosters though, I expect a few. Unless they really want to sideline me. I expect a few ways to kill people like Solars have Thunderbolt Attack Prana and a few others.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is &quot;just from looking at the solar charmset in 3e, I expect the FoS and combat tricks to get plenty of love&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T07:17:55-08:00","id":1165038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164822#post1164822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presence would also go to Endings, under the constellation of the Sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives you the opportunity to say &quot;This conversation is OVER&quot; and really have it stick","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T08:01:32-08:00","id":1165053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1165038#post1165038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives you the opportunity to say &amp;quot;This conversation is OVER&amp;quot; and really have it stick</div> </div> </div> </div>End Debate wouldn\u2019t need to remain a Bureaucracy Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T08:20:24-08:00","id":1165057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1164982#post1164982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On Athletics: it's also important to note that Athletics isn't just the ninja jump and ninja run ability. It also contains superior strength through lifting or breaking. Solars (humor me) also express Athletics through various methods of improving their combat capabilities.<br /> <br /> An Endings expression of Athletics could be an embodiment of eventuality and the forward march of time. It can represent how all things crumble to dust in the grasp of ages. It can call forth the swift end that all forms of motion face. It can also burn away the Chosen's own life force or consume their focus burning away other details for the chase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>could be</i>; <i>was</i>. It <i>was</i> that way before 2e did its thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> imagine a possible charm tree for Feats of Strength starting with a basic boost for counting strength higher for minimums. Then from there a charm that enhances suffering objects. Eventually I could see an essence 5 charm that could turn let you break an intimacy by tightly grasping a mortals hand. Maybe even end an abstract concept or break strange things normally not capable of being suffered by strength, like literally breaking enchantments. Though that's the Feats of Strength sub-tree I'm thinking about, and likely a sub-branch of that. Strength enhancing is pretty easy to think about when it comes to how to end things. </div> </div> </div>1e also had the Charm Hungry Touch, which aided in breaking objects. It also provided many hours of amusement as a similarity to Tohno Shiki breaking a chair in Tsukihime. It was not present in 2e, so all I can say is that edition was an eyesore.<br /> <br /> THAT EDITION<br /> THAT EDITION...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Charms that enhances chases are obvious. You're chasing them to end them. Maybe weird combat charms that let chases enhance a decisive attack? Nah, not too interesting but.... Hmmm...<br /> <br /> Leaping lends well to flashy assassin ninjas of course.<br /> <br /> The combat boosters though, I expect a few. Unless they really want to sideline me. I expect a few ways to kill people like Solars have Thunderbolt Attack Prana and a few others.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is &quot;just from looking at the solar charmset in 3e, I expect the FoS and combat tricks to get plenty of love&quot; </div> </div> </div>Athletics in this capacity had some carry-over in 2e, as it focused around eliding unnecessary motions and having the Sidereal skip various steps of motion to simply arrive at their objective. In spite of Athletics being under Battles in 2e, it retained these very Endings-themed Charms (Inexorable Advance and Invisible Motion), with the same prayer strip Charm at the top of the tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:30:58-08:00","id":1165384,"title":"","content":"I mean, I've got my own split (where each Maiden has both 5 Abilities in their House, and one of each of her sisters in the other Houses, giving each Sidereal a spread of 9 to choose from), but the base five per Caste lines up with Blaque's, and for basically the same reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:27:52-08:00","id":1165406,"title":"","content":"I have to say I do like being more flexible with the abilities, as Solars are, but perhaps Siddies get less of that because they've always been comparatively constrained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:51:15-08:00","id":1165414,"title":"","content":"Since Sidereals don't get Supernals (so there's no difference between caste and favoured), and don't have the Dawn Caste issue (where Dawn castes actually weren't the best pick for a combat character in 2nd ed), and they all get Martial Arts anyway (so they don't need some way to ensure they all have a combat ability or something), they don't really need it like Solars do.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:26:31-08:00","id":1165483,"title":"","content":"The real question will be when Dragonblooded comes out; if they have a variable Aspect spread, then it's almost certainly going to be a general thing going forward. If not, then yeah, probably just fixed Caste and flexible Favored.<br /> <br /> Personally, while the impetus for the idea might rest with the Dawn, I can easily see this as a more general 'thing' going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T20:19:51-08:00","id":1165508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1164747-sidereal-caste-abilities?p=1165483#post1165483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real question will be when Dragonblooded comes out; if they have a variable Aspect spread, then it's almost certainly going to be a general thing going forward. If not, then yeah, probably just fixed Caste and flexible Favored.<br /> <br /> Personally, while the impetus for the idea might rest with the Dawn, I can easily see this as a more general 'thing' going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been told the Dragon-Blooded Aspects are actually more or less teh same, just that elements bleed into different Abilities more. And the Sidereal lists so far are all more or less based on what the devs have said, which again, seems to imply they're staying fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:41:24-08:00","id":1165846,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the ones I posted were what Vance suggested; if he intended to give Sidereals more choice, I guess he'd say.<br /> <br /> DBs don't really need a spread because a)no supernals, and b)each one of them comes with a pretty wide set of caste abilities. They all have at least 1 combat, 1 social, and 1 ability that's useful outside combat and socialising.<br /> Not to mention they're not supposed to be as powerful as Solars anyway, and that Aspects, I think, are more limiting than castes in some ways.<br /> <br /> That doesn't necessarily mean no other Exalt types will have it. Just that DBs, and it seems Sidereals, won't. I imagine it'll be decided on a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, the last Vance said about Lunars is that they will get a choice, just like Solars.<br /> <br /> Solars get 20% of their abilities as caste, and get to choose these from 32% of the total number of abilities.<br /> They then get to choose another 20% of their abilities, out of all the remaining ones.<br /> <br /> Lunars will get 22.222...% of their attributes as caste, and get to choose these from 33.333...% of the total number of attributes.<br /> Then they'll get to choose another 22.222...% of their attributes as favoured, out of all the remaining ones.<br /> <br /> (If you didn't quite follow that, I mean Vance said he's currently going with Lunars choosing 2 caste attributes from a choice of 3, and then 2 favoured attributes. So very similar to how Solars do it.)<br /> <br /> This is exactly how my group has ran it for years, and it works very well.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's possible Vance has changed his mind, but I think it's a good way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:58:02-08:00","id":1165890,"title":"","content":"Thinking on the line about how abilities can say things about caste, I thought a bit about the opposite. Siderial caste can say a lot about the ability. Honestly, any ability could fit any caste and be thematically appropriate for the caste.<br /> <br /> I could see Battles Socialize by way of those businessmen and women who read and interpret the Art of War or a Book of Five Rings in their field of expertise....<br /> <br /> (Weird idea of social charms that create approximations of the combat system into the social system are flooding my mind now.... Social Initiative and Decisive Arguments.... That way leads to bad systems, ignore it.)<br /> <br /> Really any ability could be interpreted as any caste if someone is liberal enough with philosophies in universe.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm.... No. No homebrewing Battles Socialize. Its a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}